hexagon: htp: the transpose tile copy reads the source rows at the stride of a row
Fold-into: hexagon-kernels/0009

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The 2D transpose path of the copy (cpy_thread_f32_transpose2d, cpy-ops.c)
serves ggml_cont(ggml_transpose(x)) of a contiguous f32 x when the two sides
are multiples of 32. Its source is the transposed view: nb00 of the view is
one row of x, and nb01 is one element (exec_cpy selects the path only for
nb01 == 4). The kernel read the 32 rows of each source tile at the stride
nb01 / 4 = 1 float. Thus each output row c held the values x[c] thru
x[c + 31] of one row of x, and not a column of x. With this patch the stride
is nb00 / 4, one row of x.

The kernel lab (tools/htp-lab, target v81move, the release flags, v79na_1
and v81na_2): the CONT of a transposed 64 x 96 f32 matrix gave 6048 of 6144
values that differ from the source before this patch, and 0 with it. The
other cases of the target (CPY to f16, SET_ROWS, GET_ROWS, ROPE, SOFT_MAX,
GELU) give the same hashes before and after the patch, and on the two cores.

No graph of Qwen3.5 or of its vision encoder sends this shape: the delta net
runs as the fused GATED_DELTA_NET op, and the vision encoder uses
ggml_cont_3d. The CONT cases of test-backend-ops had no transposed matrix
with two sides that are multiples of 32. This patch adds four such cases
(64 x 96, 256 x 256 x 2, 32 x 32 x 3 x 2 and 1024 x 64).

The phone stage v81 (the OnePlus 13, v79, 2026-09-25): test-backend-ops CPY,
SET_ROWS, GET_ROWS and CONT on HTP0 pass 293 of 293, with the four cases.
llama-bench of the 4B Q8_0, this library against the library before the
patch, 3 alternated rounds: pp512 1003.8 against 1012.0 t/s (the standard
deviation of one run is 14 to 22 t/s), tg32 at d0 10.69 against 10.63 t/s,
tg32 at d4096 10.28 against 10.28 t/s.
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/cpy-ops.c b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/cpy-ops.c
index 6579e1a..5dc124c 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/cpy-ops.c
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/cpy-ops.c
@@ -265,7 +265,9 @@ static void cpy_thread_f32_transpose2d(unsigned int nth, unsigned int ith, void
     const HVX_Vector voff = *(HVX_Vector *) offsets;
     const uint32_t   mu   = CPY_T_TILE * VLEN;
 
-    const uint32_t src_stride = nb01 / sizeof(float);  // one row of the original matrix
+    // One row of the original matrix. The source is its transposed view, thus that row is the element stride
+    // nb00 of the view. nb01 of the view is one element.
+    const uint32_t src_stride = nb00 / sizeof(float);
     const uint32_t dst_stride = nb1  / sizeof(float);
 
     for (uint32_t i03 = 0; i03 < ne3; i03++) {
